# SPIKE — derived Gemma 4 E4B-QAT tuned for the Numen engine on M4/16GB.
#
# Why a derived model instead of base gemma4:e4b-it-qat:
#   - num_ctx: Ollama defaults context to ~4K. The Apollo stage sends a ~16K-token
#     KNOWLEDGE_CORE prompt + frame vision tokens + output. At 4K the prompt is
#     SILENTLY TRUNCATED → garbage scoring. 32K holds the largest stage with margin.
#   - temperature 0 + seed: the engine is built on determinism (same video → same
#     score). Bake the engine's seed (7) so every stage inherits it even if a call
#     forgets to pass it.
#
# Trade-off on 16GB: 32K KV cache for E4B is ~2-3GB on top of the 6.1GB weights.
# Fits alongside a Node harness (no Next dev server). If RAM-pressured, drop to
# num_ctx 16384 or swap FROM to gemma4:e2b-it-qat.
FROM gemma4:e4b-it-qat

PARAMETER num_ctx 32768
PARAMETER temperature 0
PARAMETER seed 7
# keep the whole model resident between the pipeline's many sequential stage calls
PARAMETER num_keep 24
